### IPP-304 login + session tests
### How to use: run `npm run dev` in /server, then click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.
### Uses the accounts from 303 tests:
###   ipp1 = registered AND verified,  ipp3 = registered but NOT verified (both with password secret123)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@verifiedEmail = arsalmustafa62+ipp2@gmail.com
@unverifiedEmail = arsalmustafa62+ipp3@gmail.com

### The token from request 6 is picked up automatically (no copy-paste needed).
### Run request 6 before 8.
@token = {{login.response.body.data.token}}


### 1. Login with empty body -> expect 400 "Please enter a valid email"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### 2. Wrong password -> expect 401 "Invalid email or password"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{verifiedEmail}}",
  "password": "wrongpass"
}


### 3. Email that is not registered -> expect the SAME 401 "Invalid email or password"
###    (so nobody can find out which emails are registered)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody-here@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 4. Not verified account, correct password -> expect 403 "Please verify your email..."
###    and "code": "EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED" (the frontend will show a "Resend" button for this)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{unverifiedEmail}}",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 5. Not verified account, WRONG password -> expect 401 (not 403)
###    Account status is only shown to someone who knows the password.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{unverifiedEmail}}",
  "password": "wrongpass"
}


### 6. Correct login -> expect 200 "Logged in successfully"
###    data.token = long string, data.user has NO password
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{verifiedEmail}}",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 7. /me WITHOUT token -> expect 401 "Please log in to continue"
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me


### 8. /me WITH token (from request 6) -> expect 200 with data.user (your name, email, isVerified: true)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 9. /me with a broken token -> expect 401 "Invalid login session. Please log in again"
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi


### OPTIONAL: blocked user -> expect 403 "Your account has been blocked..." with "code": "ACCOUNT_BLOCKED"
### In Atlas (Browse Collections -> users), set isBlocked: true on the ipp1 user, send request 6 again,
### then set isBlocked back to false.
